FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] phases/phase-099/REPORT.md:124 — the test gate is recorded as the literal placeholder `TOTAL_PASSED passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored`, and line 125 as `VERIFY_RESULT` — the report asserts the gate is green without recording any actual result, so the phase ships on an unsubstantiated claim — replace both with the real numbers and verify output. 
2. [MAJOR] src/runtime.rs:1881 — a deque is represented as a record chain of `{value, next}` nodes built at line 1900, so an n-element deque is an n-deep nested `Value::Record`; `collections.deque(big_list)` creates that depth in one call, and any recursive consumer (`Value` Display/PartialEq/hash, or `Arc` drop at scope exit) recurses n times and can abort the process — represent the ends with an indexed/arena structure or cap traversal depth — VERIFIED by tracing `deque_node`/`deque_value` (src/runtime.rs:1881-1905); a program that says or compares a very large deque would demonstrate it.
3. [MAJOR] src/runtime.rs:1895 — `deque_parts` supplies `Value::Nothing` for a missing `front`/`back`, so `{}` is accepted as a valid empty deque: `collections.pop_left({})` silently returns `{value: nothing, deque: ...}` and `collections.push_left({}, 1)` mints a deque instead of refusing — this contradicts “a deque is … made by collections.deque” and the reported malformed-input coverage, whose test (`tests/collections_test.rs:264`) only exercises a non-record — require both fields to be present and reject a record that was not made by the module.
4. [MINOR] tests/collections_test.rs:346 — the gate asserts `deque_time * 2 < list_time` on wall-clock measurements, which is nondeterministic: a loaded or slow CI host can fail a correct implementation, and a fast host can pass a secretly quadratic one — make this a benchmark/`#[ignore]` test or assert structural behaviour rather than elapsed time.
5. [MINOR] src/runtime.rs:1826 — `counter_parts` defaults a missing `missing` field to `0`, so `collections.count({counts: []}, 1)` silently succeeds on a record this module never made, contrary to the documented record contract and the claim that malformed counters are refused — require the field and refuse its absence.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 5
